# Founders' relay vhost for an approved shared host's Caddy instance.
# Add this block to the box's running Caddyfile and reload Caddy; this
# repository does not install it. See deploy/founders/README.md.
#
# `log { output discard }` disables the access log for this site so Caddy
# keeps no record of who connected when — the relay itself never logs tags
# (review point 5), and the vhost in front of it should not either. Marked
# "to be confirmed by the box owner": check it against however logging is
# already configured on that box (a global discard default would make this
# line redundant, not wrong).

# Review conditions (Wildbloom side, 2026-08-30): the /link WebSocket must
# be proxied with no idle timeout under the relay's 20-second ping cadence
# and with no buffering that delays frames. Caddy upgrades WebSockets on
# reverse_proxy without configuration and applies no idle timeout to an
# upgraded connection (the server's idle_timeout governs keep-alive between
# requests, not a live upgrade); flush_interval -1 disables response
# buffering so no frame waits in the proxy. Caddy still sees client IPs
# in the moment as any TLS terminator does; with the access log discarded
# it writes none.

link1.forgesworn.dev {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7443 {
		flush_interval -1
	}

	log {
		output discard
	}
}
